WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:03.620
Carrie Fisher was a whole lot more than just
Princess Leia.

00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:08.260
She was a fierce advocate for social causes,
an important voice for destigmatizing mental

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:13.679
illness, a bang-up script doctor on many of
your favorite 1990s movies, and an incredible

00:00:13.679 --> 00:00:14.679
author.

00:00:14.679 --> 00:00:19.480
It's not often that one person can be so talented
in so many fields, but Fisher was the exception.

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:23.390
She lived more in her six decades than most
of us ever will in a lifetime, and we'll never

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:25.320
know what more she had in store for us.

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:28.660
But as incredible as she was in all these
different ways, she's still best known for

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:31.960
one thing above all: her role as Leia in Star
Wars.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:35.960
Her tragic passing due to a heart attack will
almost certainly affect the future of Star

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:36.960
Wars.

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:41.420
As sad as we fans are, it's impossible not
to ask the question that's on all our minds:

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:46.020
what effect might our loss of Carrie Fisher
have on Episode VIII and Episode IX?

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:48.220
Will they change Episode VIII?

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:52.930
Shooting on director Rian Johnson's Star Wars:
Episode VIII actually wrapped back in July

00:00:52.930 --> 00:00:57.920
2016, and it’s been confirmed that Fisher
had already finished her scenes for the 2017

00:00:57.920 --> 00:00:58.920
debuting film.

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:03.040
So, however Disney decides to address Fisher's
passing, they have a decent bit of footage

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:05.360
and a good chunk of time to figure it out.

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:09.341
Productions this big usually have a tight
schedule, but as Rogue One showed us, it's

00:01:09.341 --> 00:01:14.160
not uncommon to go back for extensive reshoots
and editing in the months leading up to release.

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:18.270
If Disney decides to address Fisher's passing
in a more direct way, like having General

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:22.450
Leia be written off into retirement or die
heroically, there’s some time to tackle

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:23.450
that.

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:24.820
But, it might not be easy.

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:26.540
Going full CGI

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:31.200
As the computer-generated cameos in Rogue
One made clear, fully CGI characters can’t

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:33.670
yet seamlessly share the screen with live
actors.

00:01:33.670 --> 00:01:37.650
Though the resurrection of Peter Cushing’s
Grand Moff Tarkin was a powerful test for

00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:42.490
how far digital effects have come, the resurrected
actor still looked a bit off when acting alongside

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:44.090
living actors on screen.

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:48.000
Lucasfilm knew that Tarkin had to be in Rogue
One, since he's the commander of the Death

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:51.320
Star, and it'd be strange for him not to be
there in some capacity.

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:55.450
Even his limited screen time was a whole lot
of expensive work, so it's not really feasible

00:01:55.450 --> 00:01:57.890
to try and do this for a main character in
a film.

00:01:57.890 --> 00:02:01.800
If they try to alter or add Leia scenes digitally,
it could get tricky.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:03.290
It’s been done before

00:02:03.290 --> 00:02:07.180
If we're looking for a modern example for
how Fisher's passing might be addressed on-screen,

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:09.820
we don’t need to look further than Furious
7.

00:02:09.820 --> 00:02:15.000
To finish Paul Walker's character's story,
the studio used a mix of CGI and human stand-ins

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:19.150
to narratively retire Walker's character and
have him ride off into the sunset with his

00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:20.150
family.

00:02:20.150 --> 00:02:23.781
It’s a viable concept to apply to Episode
VIII, because Leia is obviously one of the

00:02:23.781 --> 00:02:26.280
most iconic Star Wars characters in the franchise.

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:30.320
They'll have to address her absence at some
point in the next couple of films.

00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:31.930
Who leads the Resistance next?

00:02:31.930 --> 00:02:36.650
Leia had become a revered Resistance leader
by the beginning of The Force Awakens.

00:02:36.650 --> 00:02:39.730
So in the wake of Fisher's passing, who will
lead the Resistance?

00:02:39.730 --> 00:02:44.130
Star Wars now has a fair share of strong,
young heroes, and it's not crazy to think

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:47.760
that folks like Poe Dameron, Finn, or Rey
could eventually step into that void.

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:52.650
Of course, Luke Skywalker is another obvious
option, considering he'll be returning for

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:54.310
a major role in Episode VIII.

00:02:54.310 --> 00:02:57.930
So, if they're looking for a steady hand to
take the lead, he'd certainly be a worthy

00:02:57.930 --> 00:02:59.040
successor.

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:01.680
How could this affect Luke and Kylo Ren’s
arcs?

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:05.900
Any changes the producers make to Leia's story
for the next two films will resonate with

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:06.900
her relatives.

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:10.590
Luke and Leia’s sibling bond was definitely
important to the script pages hidden deep

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:11.930
inside Lucasfilm.

00:03:11.930 --> 00:03:15.370
And the big story for Leia and Han in The
Force Awakens was the effort to turn their

00:03:15.370 --> 00:03:18.620
son back from the Dark Side… which didn’t
end so well.

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:22.630
Did Lucasfilm plan to rely on the mother-son
story between Leia and Kylo Ren?

00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:25.340
And if so, how does that story have to change
now?

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:29.390
Could Leia’s absence change Kylo's fate
before the new trilogy comes to an end?

00:03:29.390 --> 00:03:32.260
Could potentially losing both parents push
him to the Light?

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:33.790
Or further into the Dark?

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:37.860
Either way, Star Wars just won’t be the
same without Carrie Fisher.

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:39.480
"I love you."

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:40.920
"I know."

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:42.860
Thanks for watching!

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:45.159
